The Nautilus development team shared with the DevOps team requirements for new application development, setting up a Git repository for that project. 
Create a Git repository on Storage server in Stratos DC as per details given below:

Install git package using yum on Storage server.
After that, create/init a git repository named /opt/ecommerce.git (use the exact name as asked and make sure not to create a bare repository).

SOLUTION
To set up the Git repository for the Nautilus development team on the Storage server in Stratos DC, you need to install Git using yum and then initialise a non-bare repository at the exact path /opt/ecommerce.git.

📋 Step-by-Step Instructions
Log in to the Storage Server
Use SSH to connect to the storage server (the exact hostname may be ststor01 in your environment).

bash
ssh natasha@ststor01
Obtain Root Privileges
Switch to the root user or use sudo for the following commands.

bash
sudo su -
Install Git Using YUM
Install the Git package with yum. The -y flag automatically confirms the installation.

bash
yum install -y git
Create and Initialise the Non-Bare Repository
Navigate to the /opt directory and initialise the repository. Do not use the --bare flag; the task explicitly requires a non-bare repository.

bash
cd /opt
git init /opt/ecommerce.git
After running git init, a hidden .git sub-directory will be created inside /opt/ecommerce.git, confirming that a standard (non-bare) repository has been set up.

✅ Verification
You can verify the installation and repository creation with the following commands:

bash
# Check Git version
git --version

# Confirm the repository directory exists
ls -la /opt/ecommerce.git
If you see a .git directory inside /opt/ecommerce.git, the task has been completed successfully.

